ECDSA vectors made by the reference Go

Made:        2026-11-19, by `regenerate_ecdsa_go_vectors` in
             tests/go_differential.rs, through the oracle built from
             tools/oracle with go1.27.3 (dcroxide-testutil's REFERENCE_GO),
             on an x86_64 Linux desktop.
What:        216 cases of the nine ECDSA pairs of RPC_SIG_ALGS, P-256,
             P-384 and P-521 each with SHA-256, SHA-384 and SHA-512, 24 for
             each pair: Go's signatures (crypto/ecdsa's SignASN1, through
             the oracle's sig_sign) and their mutations, each with Go's
             verdict as crypto/x509 checks a certificate's signature
             (the oracle's sig_verify).  tests/ecdsa_go/mod.rs says what
             each class is and how it was made.
Why:         Wycheproof's P-521 and SHA-512 ECDSA files are not in
             tests/data/wycheproof, and were not fetched for this
             (ADR-0015, T4).

The file is the generator's JSON, pretty-printed with one trailing newline,
compressed with flate2's GzBuilder at its best level, which stores no name
and a zero time.  Go's ECDSA signatures are randomized, so a regeneration
writes other signatures and so another hash, while the count changes only
with the generator; both are pinned in tests/ecdsa_go/mod.rs.

